(A: Traditional financial advisory services suffer from accessibility barriers, high costs \(e.g.,) Tj
T* (1-2% advisory fees per year\), and fragmented analysis approaches. These issues) Tj
T* (disproportionately affect retail investors, financially illiterate users, and those from rural or) Tj
T* (semi-urban regions who often lack formal financial education and are susceptible to) Tj
T* (misleading promotions.) Tj
